<div class="flex min-h-full flex-col justify-center px-6 py-12 lg:px-8">
  <div class="sm:mx-auto sm:w-full sm:max-w-sm">
    <h1 class="text-center text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Create your account</h1>
    <%# The last screen before the commitment, and the one where somebody is most likely to be
        wondering what happens after the button. #430.

        Above the form error rather than below it: an error on this page is about the email or
        the password and wants to be the next thing read after whatever went wrong, not to have
        a price note wedged between it and the field it is about. %>
    <p class="mt-3 text-center text-sm text-gray-500">Free while it&rsquo;s in beta. No card.</p>
    <%== render('_form_error') %>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 sm:mx-auto sm:w-full sm:max-w-sm">
    <form method="post" class="space-y-8 rodauth" role="form" id="create-account-form" autocomplete="on">
    <%== rodauth.csrf_tag %>
      <div>
        <label for="email" class="block text-sm font-medium leading-6 text-gray-900">Email address</label>
        <div class="mt-2">
          <%# "email", the same token the sign-in form uses, and it has to be the same one:
              what a password manager saves here it offers back there only if both forms
              name the identifier the same way. An account here is only ever identified by
              its address, so "email" is what this field is. "username" was tried and
              reverted; the note on views/login.erb has the argument for it and says when
              it would be worth trying again. %>
          <input id="email" name="login" type="email" autocomplete="email" required
                 class="<%= field_style %> block w-full py-1.5 text-gray-900 placeholder:text-gray-400 sm:text-sm sm:leading-6">
        </div>
      </div>
      <%# There is no password box here any more. #575.

          It sat below this comment for as long as the form existed, and the comment it
          carried was about `autocomplete="new-password"` -- the instruction that asks a
          manager to generate a credential and keep it, put there after "off" made Safari and
          iOS Keychain decline to remember an account they had just watched being created.
          That argument has not stopped being true; it has moved, to views/verify-account.erb,
          along with the box, and the token is still on it.

          What moved it is that the password is now chosen after the address is confirmed.
          `verify_account` turns `create_account_set_password?` off, so a box here would be
          collected and ignored, and the account this form makes deliberately has no
          credential at all until somebody has read mail at the address -- which is what makes
          a sign-up nobody asked for a row rather than an account. app.rb has the argument and
          migrate/051 has the schema change it costs.

          The old comment also said "there is no password reset in this app", which has been
          untrue since #344 and is worth correcting on the way past rather than carrying to a
          new file: a typo costs a reset email now, not the account. %>
      <div>
        <button type="submit" class="<%= button_style %> flex w-full justify-center bg-lime-500 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold leading-6 text-gray-900 hover:bg-lime-600">Sign up</button>
      </div>
    </form>

    <p class="mt-10 text-center text-sm text-gray-500">
      Already have an account?
      <a href="/login" class="font-semibold leading-6 text-lime-700 hover:text-lime-800">Log in</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
